    '41#_': `In Shulchan Aruch seif 41 she wore garment, etc., even in seven clean days. Mishnah Lemelech wrote Tosafot Niddah 60b implies R. Yehuda doubts this; but can reject Tosafot deals such as tamei who stopped seeing such as day observer corresponding to day and did not count and one woman already counted only did not immerse — in this Tosafot doubt since in this closed opening and in this closed opening only to attribute to defective one they doubted since both anyway tamei only this already counted and this did not count — can say inapplicable to attribute defect; this is Tosafot's precision in their language doubt in partial counter or all and did not immerse can attribute to did not count at all — deals she stopped seeing and opening closed only did not begin counting yet; Shulchan Aruch deals niddah whose opening still open — thus what we attribute to her not because attributes to defective rather attributes to common frequent thing and this woman presumed blood from her — all agree plainly we attribute one with closed opening to one with open opening — plain.`,
